 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Nice that you' thinking about them. Small touch points make a big difference. Would you rather keep the comforter or buy a new one? Just few snacks make it feel like home, and cold water by the bowl is very basic. A kettle and hot drink are even cheaper but they reassure people. Leave a note instead. People panic when they see a password and don't know why. A small bouquet from you or bought off the door from a garden centre gives it the full welcome bed room touch. Lemon balm and mint in the sink help too.",
